Inputs: the project-index examples in RuboCop's specs, collected by running RSpec.
The recording includes the three index-dependent Lint cops and the other cops
whose behavior changes when a project index is available.
Corpus commit: f009b33 (see CONFORMANCE.md for the full pinned revision).
The capture retains both the inspected source and every file supplied to build_index.
Origins beginning with constructed/ are minimal regression and negative-control
inputs for file discovery, method-call shapes, comment association, constant
resolution, cross-file definitions and changes to references in other files.

Expected reports: RuboCop 1.89.0 CLI with rubydex 0.4.1, using the recorded
TargetRubyVersion and cop configuration, explicit Enabled: true and UseProjectIndex: true.
Each invocation inspects the recorded target after indexing the whole temporary project.
Reports include all offense fields and paths; normal tests need neither Ruby nor rubydex.

Regenerate the reports with:
  make project-index-fixtures

